### CHECK A: DS-001 — No Native HTML Interactive Elements
**Trigger:** Widget component render.
- Mount the chat widget React component
- Assert `document.querySelector('button, input, select, textarea, dialog')` returns `null`
- All interaction uses `@emisgroup/ui-*` equivalents
**Pass Criteria:** Zero native HTML interactive elements in rendered output.
---
### CHECK B: DS-002 — No Hardcoded Colour Values
**Trigger:** Any SCSS/CSS file in the widget component directory.
- Read all `.scss` / `.css` files
- Assert no match for `/#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,8}|rgb\(|rgba\(|hsl\(|hsla\(/`
- All colours use `var(--token-*)` design tokens
**Pass Criteria:** Zero hardcoded colour literals in style files.
---
### CHECK C: A11Y-004a — Chat Input Has Accessible Label
**Trigger:** Chat input field render.
- Render widget and run `await axe(container)`
- Assert zero violations with id `label` or `label-content-name-mismatch`
- Chat input field has `aria-label="Ask a question about EMIS interoperability"` or equivalent `aria-labelledby`
**Pass Criteria:** jest-axe `toHaveNoViolations()` passes; chat input labelled correctly.
---
### CHECK D: WCS-007a/b — All UI Text Uses i18n with British English
**Trigger:** Any user-visible text in the widget.
- Static analysis of widget `.tsx` files
- Assert zero multi-word text between `>` and `<` not wrapped in `{t(`
- Verify `src/locales/en-GB/translation.json` contains British English spellings: "colour", "centre", "grey" where applicable
- Deflection message key present in translation file
**Pass Criteria:** Zero hardcoded English strings in JSX; British English in translation JSON.
---
### CHECK E: A11Y-010 — jest-axe in Widget Component Test
**Trigger:** Widget component test file.
- Assert test file imports `axe` from `jest-axe`
- Assert test file contains `toHaveNoViolations()`
- Assert loading state uses `aria-live="polite"` or `role="status"`
- Assert error state uses `role="alert"`
**Pass Criteria:** jest-axe assertion present; live regions correctly assigned.
